              "formula_ref": "eps-overview#wq_globals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "domain_effluent",
          "label": "Effluent",
          "info": "WWTP sites whose latest effluent test met BOD, COD and TDS — the three mandatory parameters, referenced from the WWTP dashboard's own Effluent Compliance card rather than restated here.\nAdvisory parameters (pH, nitrate) are excluded, matching that card: they are reported but do not decide the verdict.\nOnly WWTP treats effluent, so no other asset appears.",
          "not_applicable_note": "This asset does not treat effluent",
          "families": [
            {
              "key": "wwtp",
              "form_id": 1748903240763,
              "params_ref": [
                "wwtp-overview#param_bod",
                "wwtp-overview#param_cod",
                "wwtp-overview#param_tds"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "donut_ohs_compliance",
          "label": "OHS Compliance",
          "info": "Share of ASSESSED sites passing, so a domain measured on part of its fleet is not reported as failing. The unmeasured remainder is the grey slice.\nEach family asks its own question: ohs_equipment_available (WWTP), has_ohs_policy (WTP), ohs_equipment (Pump Stations).\nPassing means the equipment or policy is present; every other answer counts as failing, including a pump station recording OHS equipment as 'not used'.\nRWS and EPS are absent from this donut because neither form asks an OHS question at all — see issue #34 G1 decision 2.",
          "not_applicable_note": "Neither the RWS nor the EPS form asks about OHS",
          "labels": {
            "pass": "Passing",
            "fail": "Failing",
            "notAssessed": "Not assessed"
          },
