          "id": "donut_operational_compliance",
          "label": "Operational Status",
          "info": "Share of ASSESSED sites operational, so a domain measured on part of its fleet is not reported as failing. The unmeasured remainder is the grey slice.\nEach family asks its own question: infrastructure_status (RWS), system_status (EPS), station_status (Pump Stations).\nPassing means 'operational'; every other answer counts as failing — a blocked or overflowing pump station is not operating normally.\nWWTP and WTP are absent because neither form asks a plant-level status question. WTP's has_production_constraints is not a substitute: a production constraint is not the same as a plant that is not running. See issue #34 G1 decision 1.\nThe passing count matches the functional total on the map above, which reads the same three questions.",
