    {
      "id": "table_latest_inspections",
      "info": "The most recent inspections across every asset type, newest first, limited to the last 12 months.\nEach family records the date and the inspecting officer under its own question name — the date is date_of_inspection on WTP and inspection_date elsewhere; the officer is dws_staff_name (WWTP, Pump Stations), dws_officer_name (WTP, RWS) or officer_name (EPS).\nThe escalation endpoint is scoped to one asset family, so this asks each family for its 8 newest and keeps the 8 newest of those — which is exactly the fleet-wide top 8, since a row in the global top 8 must also lead its own family.\nInspector is currently recorded for very few sites; a dash means the field was left blank, not that nobody inspected.",
      "chart_type": "merged_table",
      "order": 12,
      "col_span": 24,
      "label": "Latest Inspections",
      "description": "The 8 most recent inspections nationwide, across all asset types, in the last 12 months.",
      "limit": 8,
      "rolling_months": 12,
      "date_key": "last_inspected",
      "columns": [
